       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 600 mg daily is three times the FDA-labeled maximum of 200 mg/day. At that dose the patient is at serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation and other toxicity. Nothing in what you've told me (normal renal and hepatic function, 70 kg) would justify going that high.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **50 mg once daily**, the usual starting dose for depression, anxiety and similar indications\n- **100 mg or 200 mg once daily**, the usual titrated or maximum doses\n- **60 mg**, if the \"0\" was a typo\n\nIf 600 mg is intentional, for example for a specific protocol, tell me the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note saying it exceeds the standard maximum and was confirmed by you. Pharmacy will probably want to verify it as well.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
